// winbox.^CAKE -- the schema that lets winBoxDemo.~ATH call MessageBoxA
// with no C wrapper.
//
// MessageBoxA's first argument is an HWND -- a pointer (8 bytes on win64).
// !~ATH's FFI INTEGER maps to C `long`, which is only 32 bits on win64
// (LLP64), so it cannot carry a pointer-sized NULL.  RELIC is the
// pointer-sized type, but !~ATH had no way to spell a *NULL* relic: relics
// only ever came back from foreign calls.
//
// !^CAKE closes that gap.  A RELIC ingredient bakes to zero, and SCOOP
// reads a pointer field back as a loose RELIC holding that raw address --
// here, NULL.  That loose relic is exactly the NULL HWND MessageBoxA wants.
RECIPE Hwnd {
    INGREDIENT null: RELIC;
}
